tes the prefix, and invalidates the boundary cache — with the boundary cache adopting refresh-on-row-miss at the has/getLastInfo/getLastEntry/getEntryInfoBefore/resolveEntryWrite decision sites so a second facade over the compacted database answers correctly (the refuted stale-boundary hazard, pinned by guard); the in-memory adapter refusal is unchanged; a compacted leader completes the S4 catch-up loop for followers below the new boundary while above-boundary catch-up still batches; proven by deterministic guard scenario raft-snapshot-retention-compaction (retention sweep guards, the full compaction decision table with a no-proof-cannot-remove red direction, the compaction-catchup integration incl. second-facade and HLC non-regression and prepared-gate transitivity, plus the unweakened S1-S4 and all three gated-compaction suites) passing 3 consecutive runs.","class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"gated-compaction-guard-retained","statement":"The three snapshot-gated-compaction guard files pass unmodified; the proofless compactCommittedEntries result stays byte-identical to unsupportedRaftCompactionResult(); CL-040/041/042 repros green on every attempt."},{"id":"s6-out-of-scope","statement":"Auto-compaction triggers/cadence, scale-profile threshold calibration, production ReplicaHandler wiring, and live rebuild certification are S6 scope."}],"frontierIds":["raft-snapshot-retention-compaction-main"]}}
